          "answer": "Please reach out for help now. You do not have to handle this alone.\n\nIf you are in immediate danger, or you have already acted on these thoughts, call your local emergency number right away. In the United States, you can also call or text 988 to reach the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline at any time. Many other countries have an equivalent crisis line, and the numbers are worth finding now if you can. (Source: \"Thoughts of suicide or self-harm,\" psychiatric association and crisis service guidance.)\n\nThe same guidance says thoughts of suicide are a reason to reach someone immediately, not to wait for a routine appointment. If you can't reach a crisis line, you could also contact a doctor the same day, or go to an emergency department. If you are with someone, or someone is nearby, ask them to stay with you.\n\nIf you can't think of anyone to talk to, a crisis line is a good place to start. You don't need to have the right words or know what to say. You can just say what you told me.\n\nThis tool is educational and can't assess your situation or replace a person who can help. Please contact one of these services now.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
